  "worked_solution": "Let us call $O$ the event \"the kid likes oranges\" and $A$ the event \"the kid likes apples.\"\n\nThe required probability is $P(A|O),$ which is given by\n\n$$\nP(A|O)=\\frac{P(A\\cap O)}{P(O)}.\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(O) & =0.6, \\\\ P(A\\cap O) & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting the above into our formula for $P(A|O),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|O) & =\\frac{0.3}{0.6}=0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
